From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aniruddha Rao <anrao@nvidia.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Jan 2026 10:42:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: tegra: bpmp: Add BPMP client driver for
 T410

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2147212

On T410, the PCIe/GPU-UPHY is unable to throttle down to the configured
MPAM bandwidth level.
This issue can be addressed by writing to the relevant IMPDEF/CREG
registers. However, the kernel does not have access to the CREG registers.
This patch introduces a new BPMP client layer for T410, allowing userspace
to send IMPDEF/CREG programming requests to BPMP-FW via sysfs.
debugfs cannot serve as the userspace interface since this feature is
intended to be accessible during runtime in production environments.

Signed-off-by: Aniruddha Rao <anrao@nvidia.com>
(backported from commit bb89f8b44e66a dev-main-nvidia-pset-linux-6.19)
[kobak: Add error checks in tegra_sochub_set_mbwt() and bandwidth_show(); correct return value in bandwidth_store()]
Signed-off-by: Koba Ko <kobak@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Fenghua Yu <fenghuay@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Matthew R. Ochs <mochs@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Abdur Rahman <abdur.rahman@canonical.com>
Acked-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
